title: The New Chancellor
subtitle: A new administration takes office.
tags: event
view-if: date >= 21 and elections_held >= 1
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
face-image: img/ev_chancellery.svg
on-arrival: grand_plan += 3 if pal_chancellor; capital += 2 if rc_chancellor; faith += 2 if rc_chancellor

= The New Chancellor

[? if pal_chancellor : Supreme Chancellor Palpatine's first months are a triumph. He clears years of procedural backlog, pushes through modest anti-corruption measures, and speaks to the Senate with patience and humility. He appoints the Chagrian **Mas Amedda** as Vice Chair and a silent, pale aide named **Sly Moore** as his chief of staff. Requests for "administrative efficiency" quietly move dozens of committee staff into the Chancellor's office. ?][? if rc_chancellor : Chancellor [+ chancellor +]'s first months are a whirlwind. For the first time in a generation, reformers hold the Republic's highest office. The Caucus's patrons are delighted, and the old guilds are frightened. ?][? if not pal_chancellor and not rc_chancellor : Chancellor [+ chancellor +] takes office promising stability. Senator Palpatine, defeated but gracious, offers his "full cooperation" to the new administration. ?]

- @cooperate: [? if pal_chancellor : Cooperate with his reforms. ?][? if not pal_chancellor : Work constructively with the new government. ?]
- @scrutinise: [? if pal_chancellor : Scrutinise his appointments. ?][? if not pal_chancellor : Keep a close watch on Palpatine's circle. ?]
- @agenda: Focus on our own agenda.

@cooperate
subtitle: Good relations, and some real progress.
on-arrival: pal_relation += 5 if pal_chancellor; corruption -= 1; faith += 1; grand_plan += 1 if pal_chancellor; mod_relation += 2

The Caucus helps pass the Chancellor's first reforms. They are genuinely useful. That is the clever part.

@scrutinise
subtitle: A little evidence; a little friction.
on-arrival: evidence += 0.4; pal_relation -= 5; senate_resolve += 0.2

Caucus researchers start a quiet file on everyone in the Chancellor's circle. Most of them have no past to speak of, which is itself a little strange.

@agenda
subtitle: +1 political capital.
on-arrival: capital += 1

The Caucus gets on with its own work.
